Subject: NSS 11.4 Kbuild ccflags bridge for EXTRA_CFLAGS (Linux >= 5.3)

On Linux >= 5.3 the legacy EXTRA_CFLAGS variable is ignored for external
module builds; only ccflags-y in the module Kbuild Makefile (or KCFLAGS/
KAFLAGS on the kernel make command line) reaches the compiler. Without
this, the -I .../qca-nss-dp include path is dropped and the build fails
with: nss_phys_if.c:25:10: fatal error: nss_dp_api_if.h: No such file.

Mirror the proven 13.1 mechanism (patches/001-compat-build-system-export-
headers.patch) by bridging NSS_DRV_EXTRA_CFLAGS into ccflags-y.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -2,8 +2,10 @@
 # # Makefile for the NSS driver
 # ###################################################
 
 obj-m += qca-nss-drv.o
+
+ccflags-y += $(NSS_DRV_EXTRA_CFLAGS)
 
 #
 # Regular NSS path
 #
